          "id": "5236cd37-1588-47c4-a478-a1f0d6f4882b",
          "index": 7,
          "subtype": "QUESTION",
          "title": "Question-1",
          "tags": [
            "EXERCISE"
          ],
          "question": "Nomenclature is governed by certain universal rules. Which one of the following is contrary to the rules of nomenclature?\n\n(1) Biological names can be written in any language\n\n(2) The first word in a biological name represents the genus name, and the second is a specific epithet\n\n(3) The names are written in Latin and are italicised\n\n(4) When written by hand, the names are to be underlined",
          "answer": "Answer (1)\n\nRule for biological nomenclature: Biological names are catinised or derived from latin , which is the internationally accepted language for scientific names. It ensures uniformity and consistency across the global scientific community.",
          "options": [
            "(1) Biological names can be written in any language",
            "(2) The first word in a biological name represents the genus name, and the second is a specific epithet",
            "(3) The names are written in Latin and are italicised",
            "(4) When written by hand, the names are to be underlined"
          ],
          "prompt": "Nomenclature is governed by certain universal rules. Which one of the following is contrary to the rules of nomenclature?"
        },
        {
          "id": "2bf40353-52db-4e62-bd4f-40467c064440",
          "index": 8,
          "subtype": "QUESTION",
          "title": "Question-2",
          "tags": [
            "EXERCISE"
          ],
          "question": "The term ‘systematics’ refers to:\n\n(1) Identification and classification of plants and animals\n\n(2) Nomenclature and identification of plants and animals\n\n(3) Diversity of kinds of organisms and their relationship\n\n(4) Different kinds of organisms and their classification",
          "answer": "Answer (3)\n\n  • Systematics is the branch of biology that deals with the study of the diversity of organisms and their relationships, including classification, identification, and evolutionary history.\n  • It focuses not just on classifying organisms but also understanding their evolutionary relationships through phylogenetics.",
          "options": [
            "(1) Identification and classification of plants and animals",
            "(2) Nomenclature and identification of plants and animals",
            "(3) Diversity of kinds of organisms and their relationship",
            "(4) Different kinds of organisms and their classification"
          ],
          "prompt": "The term ‘systematics’ refers to:"
        },
        {
          "id": "860de972-d67f-4b20-999c-27efe31f65a6",
          "index": 9,
          "subtype": "QUESTION",
          "title": "Question-3",
          "tags": [
            "EXERCISE"
          ],
          "question": "The process by which anything is grouped into convenient categories based on some easily observable characters is called as :\n\n(1) Biodiversity\n\n(2) Classifications\n\n(3) Identification\n\n(4) Nomenclature",
          "answer": "Answer (2)\n\nClassification is the process of grouping organisms into convenient categories based on shared, observable characteristics, such as morphology, behavior, or genetic traits. It helps in organizing the vast diversity of life into manageable groups.",
          "options": [
            "(1) Biodiversity",
            "(2) Classifications",
            "(3) Identification",
            "(4) Nomenclature"
          ],
          "prompt": "The process by which anything is grouped into convenient categories based on some easily observable characters is called as :"
        },
        {
          "id": "1cea9c0a-3bce-4901-8278-9316d956a0b7",
          "index": 10,
          "subtype": "QUESTION",
          "title": "Question-4",
          "tags": [
            "EXERCISE"
          ],
          "question": "Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct ?\n\n(i) Classification is the providing of standardize names to the organisms such that a   particular organism known by the same all over the world.\n\n(ii) Taxonomy is the correct description of an organism and to recognition in its scientific name.\n\n(iii) The system of naming with two components (binomial nomenclature) is proposed by Carolus Linneaus.\n\n(iv) Zoological names are based on International Code for Zoological Nomenclature (ICZN).\n\n(1) Only (i)\n\n(2) Both (iii) and (iv)\n\n(3) Only (iv)\n\n(4) All of these",
          "answer": "Answer (2)\n\n  • (iii) is correct: The system of binomial nomenclature (two-part naming) was proposed by Carolus Linnaeus to standardize the naming of organisms (genus + species).\n  • (iv) is correct: Zoological names are governed by the International Code of Zoological Nomenclature (ICZN), which ensures uniformity in naming animal species.",
          "options": [
            "(1) Only",
            "(2) Both",
